	(text "DESIGN NOTE:\nVIN_ON = 1.23V * (1 + 200k / 51.1k)\nVIN_ON ~= 6.04V\n\nVIN_HYS = 5uA * 200k\nVIN_HYS ~= 1.00V\n\nVIN_OFF ~= 6.04V - 1.00V\nVIN_OFF ~= 5.04V"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 66.04 143.51 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left)
		)
		(uuid "05716d34-127e-4ea8-acef-ddf4c259319e")
	)
	(text "5V_SYS_PGOOD:\n  Allows 3.3V_SYS, TFT1V8, LCD bias, USB switch, etc. to turn on.\n\nVIN_OK / CRANK_OK:\n  Keeps high-current loads off during crank or low battery.\n  Use this to gate USB VBUS, backlight, amp enable, and maybe LCD bias.\n\nRP2040/RP2350:\n  Powered only after 3.3V_SYS is good.\n  It can observe faults and control nice-to-have behavior,\n  but the board should not depend on it to avoid brownout chaos."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 114.3 -54.61 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left)
		)
		(uuid "0af38f7c-9faf-4a2d-8d8d-4b27839f4e3e")
	)
	(text "LAYOUT NOTE:\nRoute ISP/ISN as true Kelvin traces from the two pads of R701.\nPut R702, R703, and C714 close to the TPS552892, with C714 closest to the pins.\nKeep R701 in the real output current path, not accidentally bypassed by copper pours.\nKeep R711 DNP/open unless you intentionally want cable droop compensation."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 278.13 154.94 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left)
		)
		(uuid "52d0a9c2-99b9-48f9-8e06-398132b09f2b")
	)
	(text "C2012X5R1V226M125AC"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 134.62 120.396 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 0.635 0.635)
			)
			(justify left)
		)
		(uuid "702f601a-fd86-40ca-a43a-9997eebe06a4")
	)
	(text "Layout Example"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 237.49 168.91 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 2.54 2.54)
				(thickness 0.508)
				(bold yes)
			)
			(justify left)
		)
		(uuid "a086e2a2-d32b-4eda-b234-7c3b730c6001")
	)
	(text "50 mV / 0.0068 Ω = 7.35 A"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 307.34 104.648 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
		)
		(uuid "b026272b-2fd4-4a08-916b-455598323050")
	)
	(text "Vehicle off:\nBATT+ still present, but only AP74502 + tiny always-on regulator + power manager are awake.\nTPS552892 is held off, so CM5, RP2350, LCD, touch, audio, USB, etc. are dead.\n\nACC on:\nAlways-on power manager releases TPS552892 EN/UVLO.\n+5V_SYS comes up.\n5V_SYS_GOOD enables +3V3_SYS and +1V8_SYS.\nRP2350 boots and sequences LCD/touch/backlight/amp.\n\nACC off:\nPower manager tells CM5/RP2350 to shut down.\nRP2350 immediately disables amp, backlight, LCD bias, touch, USB loads.\nPower manager waits for “halted” or timeout.\nPower manager clamps TPS552892 EN/UVLO low.\nMain system powers off."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 191.77 -54.61 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left)
		)
		(uuid "d757b283-20ab-4dbb-908d-c90b22d7d65e")
	)
